      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That perspective suggests that the existing surveillance infrastructure already diminishes personal privacy, making additional identification technology seem less intrusive. Proponents argue that augmenting current monitoring with facial recognition provides a proactive, actionable layer of security unseen with basic camera feeds. However, the philosophical difference lies in the *purpose* of the surveillance: convenience and safety versus ubiquitous, biometric data collection.",
      "source": "target",
